Yes! Well, not this camper.

252
00:13:50,340 --> 00:13:52,720
No, I'm gonna make the best of what we have.

253
00:13:53,260 --> 00:13:56,060
I'm gonna look at this glass as being half full, not half empty.

254
00:13:57,120 --> 00:13:59,900
I'm gonna accentuate the positive, not the negative.

255
00:14:00,800 --> 00:14:03,300
I'm gonna take me these lemons and I'm gonna make lemonade.

256
00:14:03,300 --> 00:14:08,820
I'm sorry. Anyone else still awake?

257
00:14:09,560 --> 00:14:11,600
Yes. How can I get to sleep?

258
00:14:11,720 --> 00:14:12,680
You guys got my bed.

259
00:14:13,380 --> 00:14:14,880
Well, I did for your mother.

260
00:14:15,100 --> 00:14:16,780
She's getting on in years.

261
00:14:19,540 --> 00:14:21,080
Oh, well, come on.

262
00:14:21,240 --> 00:14:23,420
As long as everybody's awake, why don't we talk?

263
00:14:24,020 --> 00:14:24,980
You mean to each other?

264
00:14:25,640 --> 00:14:28,580
Well, Ben, families have been known to talk to each other, you know.

265
00:14:28,780 --> 00:14:30,140
Yeah, sure, on TV.

266
00:14:30,140 --> 00:14:32,860
Well, all right, all right, then let's pretend we're on TV.

267
00:14:32,940 --> 00:14:33,840
Why don't we give it a try?

268
00:14:33,840 --> 00:14:35,340
Come on, Carol, go first.

269
00:14:36,200 --> 00:14:38,260
Okay. What do you want me to say?

270
00:14:38,460 --> 00:14:40,760
Well, whatever's important to you, whatever you're feeling.

271
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:42,880
Whatever weighs heaviest on your mind.

272
00:14:44,040 --> 00:14:45,560
Oh, here we go.

273
00:14:45,600 --> 00:14:46,660
Another fat joke.

274
00:14:47,460 --> 00:14:52,980
Why can't anybody just accept the fact that I have lost 33 and a third pounds?

275
00:14:53,940 --> 00:14:56,000
Okay, we won't start with Carol.

276
00:14:56,420 --> 00:14:58,720
Ben? Well, I've got a good joke.

277
00:14:58,720 --> 00:15:00,400
if bodily fluids don't offend you.

278
00:15:01,700 --> 00:15:03,580
Okay, we won't start with Ben.

279
00:15:03,880 --> 00:15:06,860
Mike. Look, I'm not saying anything until I get my bed back.

280
00:15:07,680 --> 00:15:09,520
Okay, we won't start with Mike.

281
00:15:09,960 --> 00:15:13,760
Maggie. I don't appreciate that crack about me getting on in years.

282
00:15:14,320 --> 00:15:15,720
Good idea. I'll start.

283
00:15:16,940 --> 00:15:20,880
You guys remember when the last time was that we all spent a night together in one

284
00:15:20,880 --> 00:15:21,660
room? Ha -ha -ha.

285
00:15:21,660 --> 00:15:23,760
Remember? It was 10 years ago.

286
00:15:23,760 --> 00:15:25,500
That was at your Aunt Rose's funeral.

287
00:15:25,700 --> 00:15:27,040
Now, that was a fun time.

288
00:15:29,440 --> 00:15:31,500
Jason. I don't mean the funeral was fun, Meg.

289
00:15:31,500 --> 00:15:34,860
I mean the fact that we had to spend the night in your Uncle Bobby's bomb shelter.

290
00:15:34,920 --> 00:15:37,000
Remember that? Remember what we did?

291
00:15:37,060 --> 00:15:38,040
We played games.

292
00:15:38,140 --> 00:15:39,340
We sang songs.

293
00:15:39,820 --> 00:15:42,880
We invaded the emergency rations and we gorged ourselves.

294
00:15:42,920 --> 00:15:47,340
Remember that? Your mom got all tanked up and set off Uncle Bobby's flares.

295
00:15:49,200 --> 00:15:50,160
I did not.

296
00:15:50,160 --> 00:15:51,100
I know you didn't.

297
00:15:51,160 --> 00:15:52,900
I made that up just to make this more interesting.

298
00:15:54,460 --> 00:15:55,860
Dad, is there a point to this?

299
00:15:56,360 --> 00:15:59,540
Yes, Mike. The point is, we were a family then.

300
00:16:00,140 --> 00:16:02,100
You know, we didn't want to spend the night together.

301
00:16:02,260 --> 00:16:06,700
We're all crowded in one room underground with no air and Mike's feet.

302
00:16:08,580 --> 00:16:09,960
But the point is, we did it.

303
00:16:09,980 --> 00:16:11,840
You know, we made the most of it.

304
00:16:11,900 --> 00:16:17,060
And it just occurred to me that, uh, I don't know, maybe, maybe this is the last

305
00:16:17,060 --> 00:16:20,980
time we'll ever spend a night together, alone in one room.

306
00:16:21,940 --> 00:16:23,420
See, you mean you get in the hotel room tomorrow night?

307
00:16:23,560 --> 00:16:25,660
Great. He needed to wait.

308
00:16:28,440 --> 00:16:32,400
Maggie, Maggie. When did these kids change?

309
00:16:33,640 --> 00:16:46,860
Rrrrr. Yo, Mikey, can you spare me a ten?

310
00:16:47,320 --> 00:16:49,060
What? What? Oh, I'm sorry.

311
00:16:49,080 --> 00:16:50,300
I didn't realize you were sleeping with your mother.

312
00:16:51,640 --> 00:17:04,420
Ah! Hey, Michael, what's happening?

313
00:17:05,160 --> 00:17:07,060
Well, you're pretty much looking at it, Ed.

314
00:17:07,740 --> 00:17:08,700
Eddie, what are you doing?

315
00:17:09,160 --> 00:17:11,160
Well, actually, Michael, I was wondering if you can lend me a ten.

316
00:17:11,360 --> 00:17:13,100
Uh, yeah. At four in the morning?

317
00:17:13,740 --> 00:17:15,000
Uh, look, all I got's a twenty.

318
00:17:15,100 --> 00:17:15,560
Oh, that'll do.

319
00:17:15,820 --> 00:17:18,360
Well, wait, for me you had three, for him you've got twenty?

320
00:17:18,520 --> 00:17:20,140
Well, he pays me back.

321
00:17:21,480 --> 00:17:22,400
Thank you, Michael.

322
00:17:22,660 --> 00:17:24,160
Yeah. This is really neat.

323
00:17:24,400 --> 00:17:26,620
You know, my family never sleeps all together in the same room.

324
00:17:27,500 --> 00:17:29,560
Wow, Carol, you're developing quite nicely.

325
00:17:35,420 --> 00:17:37,360
Oh, I can't sleep on this floor.

326
00:17:37,480 --> 00:17:38,780
Things are crawling on me.

327
00:17:39,060 --> 00:17:40,420
Oh, I'm sorry, honey.

328
00:17:40,600 --> 00:17:41,520
Just climb in.

329
00:17:41,720 --> 00:17:42,900
Oh. Wait a second.

330
00:17:43,040 --> 00:17:45,800
The snowball gets bedded, I have to suffer on the floor?

331
00:17:45,880 --> 00:17:47,780
Get it. Hey, wait a minute.

332
00:17:47,840 --> 00:17:49,040
Wait a whole time out.

333
00:17:49,040 --> 00:17:51,780
I'm the one who owns the bed and you guys are gonna sleep in it?

334
00:17:51,860 --> 00:17:52,860
I'm gonna sleep on the floor?

335
00:17:53,180 --> 00:17:54,440
No way! Make room.

336
00:17:55,040 --> 00:17:56,500
Oh, come on.

337
00:17:56,640 --> 00:17:59,120
Ow! Hey, Mike, that's my foot, asshole!

338
00:17:59,140 --> 00:18:01,420
I'm sorry. Yeah, well, who's got their elbow in my foot?

339
00:18:01,900 --> 00:18:03,620
Somebody needs to cut their toenail.

340
00:18:03,800 --> 00:18:04,820
I'm sorry, Mike.

341
00:18:05,420 --> 00:18:07,680
You can't have this many people in this bed.

342
00:18:07,720 --> 00:18:10,100
Yeah, he likes to have twice as many people in this baby.

343
00:18:13,220 --> 00:18:14,540
Oh, don't worry.

344
00:18:14,600 --> 00:18:15,680
Don't worry. They're all guys.

345
00:18:18,080 --> 00:18:19,020
No, I mean...

346
00:18:19,020 --> 00:18:20,880
Wait, babe, did you hit the bed?

347
00:18:21,140 --> 00:18:25,720
Heck no. Wait a minute, we're not wetting the bed, the bed's wetting us.

348
00:18:25,900 --> 00:18:28,800
What? Oh my god!

349
00:18:30,160 --> 00:18:30,320
Oh my god!

350
00:18:30,320 --> 00:18:32,140
Come on! Hey, it's a box!

351
00:18:32,360 --> 00:18:34,020
I'm just trying to play it out!

352
00:18:34,180 --> 00:18:37,760
That was Mike who broke the water bag's back, not Slim's belt, Carol!

353
00:18:37,880 --> 00:18:39,140
Oh, Carol, shut up!

354
00:18:39,380 --> 00:18:43,400
Oh, nice! The genius who cancels the credit card tells his daughter to shut up!

355
00:18:43,620 --> 00:18:47,920
I did what I had to do, and I tell you, staying here It's a lot better than

356
00:18:47,920 --> 00:18:49,140
borrowing money from love.

357
00:18:49,220 --> 00:18:50,640
Oh, so it makes sense.

358
00:18:50,920 --> 00:18:52,320
He wouldn't like it to you.

359
00:18:52,400 --> 00:18:54,160
Oh, yeah? Well, I chose what you know.

360
00:18:54,440 --> 00:18:55,980
I didn't even ask him.

361
00:18:56,040 --> 00:18:57,560
What? Yeah, that's right.

362
00:18:57,580 --> 00:18:58,940
A man has his pride.

363
00:18:59,060 --> 00:19:01,600
You mean we weren't forced to stay in this place with Charles?

364
00:19:01,660 --> 00:19:02,940
That's right. I chose to.

365
00:19:03,020 --> 00:19:06,980
But that was before I so stupidly thought that we might enjoy this and have a little

366
00:19:06,980 --> 00:19:09,520
family fun. Ha ha ha ha ha ha.

367
00:19:09,940 --> 00:19:11,200
Is everybody gonna just stand there?

368
00:19:11,240 --> 00:19:12,740
You're gonna help me drink my bed.

369
00:19:12,880 --> 00:19:15,480
Oh, this is terrible.

370
00:19:17,200 --> 00:19:21,460
Oh! Where the hell am I?

371
00:19:24,280 --> 00:19:26,140
Jason, what are you doing out here?

372
00:19:26,180 --> 00:19:26,540
I don't know.

373
00:19:26,600 --> 00:19:27,260
I got confused.

374
00:19:27,400 --> 00:19:27,860
I got lost.

375
00:19:27,920 --> 00:19:29,300
I thought I was heading for the steps.

376
00:19:30,200 --> 00:19:32,060
Didn't this look like a pretty small door?

377
00:19:33,800 --> 00:19:35,020
Maggie, I should warn you.

378
00:19:35,020 --> 00:19:37,480
If you're coming out here, we may actually have to converse.

379
00:19:37,880 --> 00:19:40,260
And as you know, that's something this family does not do.

380
00:19:41,980 --> 00:19:46,460
Okay, Jason. You want to talk about this, are you still wallowing in your melodrama?

381
00:19:46,620 --> 00:19:48,420
I'm still wallowing, thank you.

382
00:19:49,260 --> 00:19:53,760
I'll be fine, Maggie, as soon as I accept and realize the fact that the family that

383
00:19:53,760 --> 00:19:55,220
I once knew and loved is gone.

384
00:19:55,380 --> 00:19:57,300
Oh, geez. Oh, Maggie, come on.

385
00:19:57,300 --> 00:19:59,840
We used to appreciate the simple things.

386
00:20:01,400 --> 00:20:02,440
Shut up there.

387
00:20:02,440 --> 00:20:12,160
I'm talking. You know, I don't think I've been up on this balcony since the day we

388
00:20:12,160 --> 00:20:12,920
moved in here.

389
00:20:14,420 --> 00:20:20,000
Remember, Jason, we climbed up here to look at our brand -new house, and you were

390
00:20:20,000 --> 00:20:23,880
complaining about how much more the movers charged us than their estimate.

391
00:20:26,340 --> 00:20:28,400
I'd still say those guys ripped us off.

392
00:20:29,860 --> 00:20:32,260
Jason, honey, I think you're missing the spirit here.

393
00:20:33,100 --> 00:20:34,580
Remember what we talked about that day?

394
00:20:37,100 --> 00:20:41,180
Hmm. Yeah, we talked about having all these rooms, and would we ever have enough

395
00:20:41,180 --> 00:20:42,280
kids to fill them?

396
00:20:42,280 --> 00:20:45,240
Hm. Well, we sure have come a long way, haven't we?

397
00:20:45,260 --> 00:20:45,940
I don't know.

398
00:20:46,040 --> 00:20:51,580
We're standing on the same balcony, overlooking the same house, and watching those

399
00:20:51,580 --> 00:20:53,500
rooms empty one by one.

400
00:20:54,820 --> 00:20:57,460
Oh, honey, we can't have time stand still.

401
00:20:57,600 --> 00:21:00,860
No, no, but I just feel sad.

402
00:21:02,320 --> 00:21:04,780
Jason, you like to be sad.

403
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:07,800
Yeah? Yeah, but come on, face it, honey.

404
00:21:07,800 --> 00:21:09,740
Things are never going to be the way they were.

405
00:21:09,740 --> 00:21:12,240
I just feel I've lost something.

406
00:21:13,440 --> 00:21:17,700
Honey, how come when you remember Aunt Rose's funeral and that night in the bomb

407
00:21:17,700 --> 00:21:21,940
shelter, you don't remember Carol and Ben fighting all night long?

408
00:21:22,100 --> 00:21:25,840
Or Mike locking Carol out, yelling, "'Nuke her, nuke her

409
00:21:27,060 --> 00:21:30,120
Or Ben setting off emergency flares at 3 in the morning?

410
00:21:30,140 --> 00:21:31,400
Yeah, I remember all that stuff.

411
00:21:31,460 --> 00:21:32,600
Maggie, it was a great night.

412
00:21:32,780 --> 00:21:35,340
Back then, you said Aunt Rose had a better weekend than we did.

413
00:21:36,600 --> 00:21:38,040
Yeah, I didn't mean that.

414
00:21:38,040 --> 00:21:39,140
Oh, yes, you did.

415
00:21:39,700 --> 00:21:44,860
Sweetheart, you are one of those rare individuals that needs 10 years to look back

416
00:21:44,860 --> 00:21:46,820
on something before he appreciates it.

417
00:21:46,880 --> 00:21:50,720
In the year 2000, you'll look back on this as the day Carol crashed through the

418
00:21:50,720 --> 00:21:54,440
ceiling, our credit cards were confiscated at gunpoint, and Mike's waterbed turned

419
00:21:54,440 --> 00:21:55,760
into Old Faithful.

420
00:21:57,080 --> 00:21:59,000
And you'll remember it fondly.

421
00:22:01,960 --> 00:22:07,520
I will. Well, I'm sure glad I married you.

422
00:22:08,720 --> 00:22:10,100
See what I mean?

423
00:22:10,440 --> 00:22:12,520
21 years and you're just starting to get it.

424
00:22:13,900 --> 00:22:17,520
And when I do look back on this night, it's gonna be with you.

425
00:22:18,100 --> 00:22:19,720
Right here from the same balcony.

426
00:22:29,600 --> 00:22:31,040
We'll be back in a moment.
